<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s258S">And <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s258w2">if</span> you try to <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w1">agree</span> to these absurdities, you are <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s258w3">wrong</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s258w9">for</span> the quality of being <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w4"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s258w5">pus</span> and <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s258w6">blood</span></span> is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w8">incompatible</span> with the quality of being either one of the other two <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w7">substances</span> mentioned. <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s258w10">Moreover</span>, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s258w11">the quality of being water and the quality of not being water</span> are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w13">directly incompatible</span> in such a way that, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s258w12">if something exists and lacks one of these qualities, it must then possess the other</span>.</span>
